## Code Style and Structure
- Write concise, technical TypeScript code with accurate examples
- Use functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid classes
- Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError)
- Structure repository files as follows:
```

├── src/
    ├── components/         # Shared components based on antd ui
    ├── assets/             # static assets
    ├── common/             # Helper functions
        ├── auth/           # auth related functions
        ├── context/     # react context
        ├── enum/           # global enum api
        ├── hooks/          # custom hooks
        ├── i18n/           # translation
        ├── permissionForm/ # permission form for userSetting
        ├── service/        # global service api
        ├── utils/          # global utils
    ├── feature/            # main feature for the page of the project display on the sidebar
    ├── type/           # global type
    ├── typing/         # typing for the project

## Tech Stack
- React
- TypeScript
- antd ui

## Naming Conventions
- Use camelCase for directories in features (e.g., features/adjustmentLogReport)
- Use PascalCase for files and fitting component name in directories under features (e.g., features/adjustmentLogReport/AdjustmentLogReportFilter.tsx)
- Favor named exports for components and utilities
- Use PascalCase for component files (e.g., VisaForm.tsx)
- Use camelCase for utility files (e.g., formValidator.ts)

## TypeScript Usage
- Use TypeScript for all code; prefer interfaces over types
- Avoid enums; use const objects with 'as const' assertion
- Use functional components with TypeScript interfaces
- Define strict types for message passing between different parts of the extension
- Avoid try/catch blocks unless there's good reason to translate or handle error in that abstraction
- Use explicit return types for all functions

## State Management
- Use Redux for global state when needed

## Syntax and Formatting
- Use array function for pure functions
- Avoid unnecessary curly braces in conditionals
- Use declarative TSX
- Implement proper TypeScript discriminated unions for message types

## UI and Styling
- Use antd ui for components

## Error Handling
- Use Try Catch for error handling 

## Testing
- No testing for Now


## Security
- Implement Content Security Policy
- Sanitize user inputs
- Handle sensitive data properly

## Git Usage
Commit Message Prefixes:
- "fix:" for bug fixes
- "feat:" for new features
- "perf:" for performance improvements
- "docs:" for documentation changes
- "style:" for formatting changes
- "refactor:" for code refactoring
- "test:" for adding missing tests
- "chore:" for maintenance tasks

Rules:
- Use lowercase for commit messages
- Keep the summary line concise

## Documentation
- Maintain clear README with setup instructions
- Document API interactions and data flows
- Don't include comments unless it's for complex logic

## Development Workflow
- Implement proper code review process

## How to create a new feature
   ### part 1: create a new feature
    1. create a new blank camelCase for the featureName folder under src/features
    2. create a new blank PascalCase for the featureName.tsx file under src/features/featureName -- this is the main page of the feature
    3. create a new blank PascalCase for the featureNameFilter.tsx file under src/features/featureName -- this is the filter component of the feature
    4. create a new blank PascalCase for the featureNameTable.tsx file under src/features/featureName -- this is the table component of the feature
    5. create a new blank PascalCase for the api.ts file under src/features/featureName, use rootApi.injectEndpoints to create the api -- this is the api of the feature
    6. create a new blank PascalCase for the type.ts file under src/features/featureName -- this is the type of the feature

   ### part 2: create a new route for the feature
    !important: if not provider the functionId for the featureName.tsx and its position in the menu, then response to the chat please provide the functionId and its position in the menu with picture
    1. provider the functionId for the featureName.tsx file and according the image of the menu for the featureName position under src/app/constants/paths.ts
      - drawPrizeReport is under marketing so the path is marketing/drawPrizeReport
      - the feature is consist of 3 parameters: sub(optional if not have sub, then it's empty), root, functionId
    2. lazy import the featureName.tsx file under src/app/routes/index.tsx    
      - webpackChunkName: pascalCase of 'featureName'
    3. add the featureName.tsx file to the MENU_MAPPING constant under src/app/constants/menuMapping.tsx
     - path: `${NEW_SITE_PREFIX_URL}/${paths.featureName.root}`
     - element: <AuthRequire functionId={paths.featureName.functionId}> according the image of the menu for the featureName position under src/app/constants/paths.tsx
    4. create a new object in MENU_MAPPING for the react-router-dom path and element under src/contants/menuMapping.tsx -- pathMode: 'NewAdmin' ,internalPath is their [parent path/featureName]
